stateDiagram-v2
    direction LR

    [*] --> DRAFT: CR1 maker holds P on the object in scope
    DRAFT --> DISCARDED: CR3 maker discards
    DRAFT --> CHECK_PENDING: CR2 submit, validations and consent gate pass
    CHECK_PENDING --> CHECK_PENDING: CR11 SLA breached, backup checker assigned
    CHECK_PENDING --> APPROVED: CR4 distinct checker approves on a current base
    CHECK_PENDING --> REJECTED: CR9 checker rejects with a reason
    CHECK_PENDING --> WITHDRAWN: CR10 maker withdraws
    CHECK_PENDING --> STALE: CR12 another change on the object took effect first
    STALE --> DRAFT: CR13 maker rebases on the new base
    APPROVED --> VERIFYING: CR5 external verification needed
    APPROVED --> EFFECTIVE: CR8 no verification needed
    VERIFYING --> EFFECTIVE: CR6 verification passes
    VERIFYING --> VERIFICATION_FAILED: CR7 verification fails, prior value stays
    EFFECTIVE --> [*]
    DISCARDED --> [*]
    REJECTED --> [*]
    WITHDRAWN --> [*]
    VERIFICATION_FAILED --> [*]

    note right of CHECK_PENDING
        The maker, the subject of the change and
        anyone holding the maker's role on this
        instance can never approve it. With no
        eligible checker it waits under FOUR_EYES_GAP.
    end note

    note right of APPROVED
        The object's value is unchanged until
        EFFECTIVE. An effective date inside a
        LOCKED month spawns a correction run
        as a diff, never a mutation.
    end note
